    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured audit event in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`, the single create path for owners.\n\n**What changed:**\n\n1. **Monotonic sequence** \u2014 added a static `AtomicLong OWNER_CREATED_SEQ` so each successful create stamps a monotonically increasing `seq` in creation order (concurrency-safe, matching the existing `IDEMPOTENT_CREATES` pattern).\n\n2. **Event emission** \u2014 after the existing human-readable audit line in `createOwner(...)`, a new `emitOwnerCreatedEvent(owner)` publishes an immutable JSON event to the same `AUDIT` logger:\n   ```json\n   {\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n   ```\n   with the field order the spec requires: `seq`, `ownerId`, `customerCode`, `membershipLevel`, `event:'OWNER_CREATED'`.\n\n3. **The identity seam** \u2014 the `customerCode` field is populated via a `primaryIdentifier(Owner)` helper that today returns `owner.getCustomerCode()`. This is the one place that decides which field is primary, so when the customer code is later unified into the member id, returning the member id from this helper makes the event carry the memberId instead \u2014 the event shape stays identical, exactly as the spec anticipates.\n\n4. **`jsonString(...)`** escapes JSON-significant characters and renders `null` correctly, keeping the emitted event valid JSON regardless of the identifier's contents.\n\nNote I used SLF4J's `{}` placeholders \u2014 the literal JSON braces (`{\"`, `\"}`) aren't empty-brace tokens so they pass through untouched, while the four `{}` bind the values.\n\nThe target test `coreEventCarriesIdAndIdentifier` passes (it asserts one `AUDIT` line contains `OWNER_CREATED`, the owner id, and the `customerCode`), and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
